1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,073
This is the Autonomous Lead Enrichment Agent.

2
00:00:03,193 --> 00:00:06,374
It turns company domains into structured business intelligence.

3
00:00:06,494 --> 00:00:12,299
This walkthrough shows actual project files and captured terminal results, with waiting time removed.

4
00:00:13,819 --> 00:00:18,277
The project separates crawling, cleaning, extraction, and orchestration.

5
00:00:18,397 --> 00:00:23,866
A simple JSON file supplies the three assignment targets: Postman, Supabase, and Vapi.

6
00:00:23,986 --> 00:00:27,561
The README documents environment setup and local execution.

7
00:00:29,081 --> 00:00:33,099
The command selects NVIDIA and enables the free tier only guard.

8
00:00:33,219 --> 00:00:37,352
Playwright renders JavaScript pages and discovers relevant company links.

9
00:00:37,472 --> 00:00:43,787
These terminal excerpts come from a real run, with concurrent processing and up to eight attempted pages per company.

10
00:00:46,081 --> 00:00:51,561
The cleaner removes scripts, styles, SVG elements, and navigation boilerplate.

11
00:00:51,681 --> 00:00:56,813
It extracts readable text while preserving contact signals and profile associations.

12
00:00:56,933 --> 00:00:59,615
A bounded context reduces token use.

13
00:00:59,735 --> 00:01:04,483
The language model receives clean evidence, rather than raw HTML trees.

14
00:01:06,003 --> 00:01:15,941
Pydantic defines the required fields: a two sentence overview, target audience, public emails, leadership details, and confidence between zero and one.

15
00:01:16,061 --> 00:01:23,329
The extractor validates the returned schema and checks that names, roles, and contact details have supporting evidence.

16
00:01:24,849 --> 00:01:28,344
An earlier attempt encountered an NVIDIA server error for Postman.

17
00:01:28,464 --> 00:01:31,645
Supabase and Vapi still completed and saved their results.

18
00:01:31,765 --> 00:01:35,074
The pipeline records failures and uses bounded retries.

19
00:01:35,194 --> 00:01:41,266
Missing pages, browser timeouts, and bot challenges are also handled without cancelling other companies.

20
00:01:42,786 --> 00:01:45,990
Here is the actual Postman output from the completed batch.

21
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:52,647
It contains the company overview, intended audience, public contact emails, and leadership profiles.

22
00:01:52,767 --> 00:01:58,885
Source pages and crawl errors remain attached, so a reviewer can inspect where the information came from.

23
00:02:00,786 --> 00:02:04,153
The combined JSON contains records for all three targets.

24
00:02:04,273 --> 00:02:06,247
Missing information is left empty.

25
00:02:06,367 --> 00:02:13,089
In this evidence, Vapi has no supported leadership entries, and the optional Supabase profile search was blocked.

26
00:02:13,209 --> 00:02:16,576
Confidence reflects the completeness of the available evidence.

27
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:21,103
The saved output verifier is run against this batch.

28
00:02:21,223 --> 00:02:27,387
It checks the schema, two sentence summaries, entity evidence, page limits, and token totals.

29
00:02:27,507 --> 00:02:32,883
The displayed validation is from an actual terminal execution, and all three records pass.

30
00:02:34,403 --> 00:02:38,582
The summary records actual token usage and estimated cost per domain.

31
00:02:38,702 --> 00:02:42,650
The zero dollar estimate uses the configured NVIDIA free tier rates.

32
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:49,736
The project includes modular code, dependencies, tests, setup instructions, and a three company sample output.

33
00:02:49,856 --> 00:02:50,552
Thank you.
